      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-243106",
      ":question/problem": "In a small group on a messaging platform, users create private chats to send direct messages to one another. Each private chat connects exactly two users. The group manager reports that, during a specific time period, exactly $5$ users participated in $3$ private chats each, while the remaining users each participated in $6$ private chats. Select the correct reasoning options to explain why the report contains an error.Let's consider a graph in which a vertex represents a {{field-1}}, and each edge represents a {{field-2}}.\n\nWe are told that our graph must contain an\n{{field-3}}\nnumber of vertices (namely, {{field-4}})\nwith an\n{{field-5}}\ndegree of {{field-6}}.\nHowever, this contradicts the\n{{field-7}}, which states that the number of vertices with {{field-8}} degrees must be {{field-9}}.\n\nTherefore, the situation described in the report is {{field-10}}."
    },
