      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-257926",
      ":question/problem": "In a group project, students collaborate in subgroups. Each subgroup consists of exactly two students. The teacher reports that $7$ students participate in $3$ subgroups each, while the remaining students each participate in $4$ subgroups. Select the correct reasoning options to explain why the report contains an error.Let's consider a graph in which a vertex represents a {{field-1}}, and each edge represents a {{field-2}}.\n\nWe are told that our graph must contain an\n{{field-3}}\nnumber of vertices (namely, {{field-4}})\nwith an\n{{field-5}}\ndegree of {{field-6}}.\nHowever, this contradicts the\n{{field-7}}, which states that the number of vertices with {{field-8}} degrees must be {{field-9}}.\n\nTherefore, the situation described in the report is {{field-10}}."
